  "question": {
    "text": "Let $P$ be the foot of the perpendicular from the point $Q(10,-3,-1)$ on the line $\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y-2}{-1}=\\frac{z+1}{-2}$. Then the area of the right angled triangle $P Q R$, where $R$ is the point $(3,-2,1)$, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "E0HTt",
      "text": "$9 \\sqrt{15}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "N7Wxa",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{30}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4fjTg",
      "text": "$8 \\sqrt{15}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wY1r1",
      "text": "$3 \\sqrt{30}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn.quizrr.in/question-assets/jee_main_pyq/N6AY-e_ilcleaUBp105pn4vdNn1IG20dx427cO8pHSk.original.fullsize.png\"><br>$\\begin{aligned}\r\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{x}-3}{7}=\\frac{\\mathrm{y}-2}{-1}=\\frac{\\mathrm{z}+1}{-2}=\\lambda \\\\\r\n& \\Rightarrow 7 \\lambda+3,-\\lambda+2,-2 \\lambda-1 \\\\\r\n& \\text {dr's of QP } \\Rightarrow 7 \\lambda-7,-\\lambda+5,-2 \\lambda\r\n\\end{aligned}$\r\nNow\r\n$\\begin{aligned}\r\n& (7 \\lambda-7) \\cdot 7-(-\\lambda+5)+(2 \\lambda) \\cdot 2=0 \\\\\r\n& 54 \\lambda-54=0 \\Rightarrow \\lambda=1 \\\\\r\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{P}=(10,1,-3) \\\\\r\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{PQ}}=-4 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+2 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} \\\\\r\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{PR}}=-7 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-3 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+4 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} \\\\\r\n& \\text {Area } =\\frac{1}{2}\\left| \\begin{array}{ccc}\r\n\\mathrm{i} & \\mathrm{j} & \\mathrm{k} \\\\\r\n0 & -4 & 2 \\\\\r\n-7 & -3 & 4\r\n\\end{array} \\right|=3 \\sqrt{30}\r\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
